    {
      "suggestedName": "Paper Abstract Summary",
      "conceptualOrigin": null,
      "category": "abstract",
      "visualMetaphor": "Deleterious oral habits persisting in children over three years old lead to significant physical and psychological issues. Existing interventions often lack engagement and continuous methods for the 4-7 age group to consciously abandon these habits. This paper introduces 'Duda: The Little Tooth's Guardian,' a digital game-based methodology designed as an engaging, playful, and continuous intervention to promote changes in these habits through an interactive narrative, minigames, and a reward system, involving family and dental professionals.",
